00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.400
Boa Hancock isn’t one of the most&nbsp;
popular characters in One Piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.200
because she is beautiful or because shippers have&nbsp;
taken over the fandom, but because she represents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.320
the core values and themes of the story like&nbsp;
almost no other character. And in this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:22.080
I will tell you exactly what those characteristics&nbsp;
are, how Oda designed Boa Hancock to tie together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.360
some of the most high-stake parts of the story&nbsp;
before, during and after the time skip and why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.240
I believe that the snake princess will return&nbsp;
to the story sooner than we all might think.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.760
On the most superficial level, Boa Hancock is&nbsp;
a character of extremes. When we first meet her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.560
in the story, she appears to be extremely&nbsp;
arrogant, spoiled and cold hearted. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.640
falling in love with Luffy, this quickly changes&nbsp;
from total disdain to suddenly total devotion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.280
caring and thinking about nothing but Luffy.&nbsp;
When looking at it from this perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.080
it’s quite easy to understand, why some&nbsp;
people are confused why Hancock enjoys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:04.320
such popularity in the fandom. After all she seems&nbsp;
to go from saltily cold to clumsily lovestruck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.120
giving her character an annoying twist, just so&nbsp;
the main character can progress in the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.720
Of course the only logical reason why people&nbsp;
like her character then, must be her looks. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:20.240
while Hancock has undoubtedly one of the best&nbsp;
visual female designs in the story, her charm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.680
comes form a much more fundamental and emotional&nbsp;
place. Because most of the time, whenever Oda does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.360
something that appears to be questionable to&nbsp;
fans, he usually does so for a deeper reason.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.520
And as so often is the case in One Piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:39.840
the key to understanding her&nbsp;
character lies in her backstory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.760
As you might remember, one of the big reveals&nbsp;
about Hancock is the mark that is burned on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.560
her back. As a child, she and her two sisters&nbsp;
were abducted by slave traders and sold to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.400
Tenryubito. Since it’s still a Shounen manga, Oda&nbsp;
only hints at all the horrors that the 3 sisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.440
must have gone through during their captivity,&nbsp;
but he leaves no doubt that these experiences left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:09.040
them deeply traumatized. Coming from a nation of&nbsp;
women, this first encounter with the world of men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.760
obviously led to even deeper hatred and rejection&nbsp;
towards any men, than originally was already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:23.680
the case. But the consequences of this past&nbsp;
reach even deeper. Hancock is characterized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.800
as extremely cruel and cold-hearted. She is&nbsp;
convinced that her beauty is enough to let her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.240
get away with anything she wants. And if that&nbsp;
ever shouldn’t be enough, which it usually is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:40.240
she still has her power. Oda caricatures this&nbsp;
literal heartlessness as her kicking puppies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:46.080
and baby seals, but it’s meant to embody the pain,&nbsp;
vulnerability and insecurity deep inside of her.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.720
For years, Hancock as a slave had to&nbsp;
be fully subservient to her masters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.880
being treated as nothing but an object.&nbsp;
And so after being freed by Fisher tiger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.320
it is only natural that she&nbsp;
fully embraced her new freedom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:04.560
never to let go of it again. That also means&nbsp;
that accepting or even acknowledging any sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.520
help from others is impossible, as it would make&nbsp;
her indebted to that person and give up even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:16.480
tiniest bit of control. This is for instance&nbsp;
why she can’t seem to thank elder Nyon. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.160
yet, the mark of the celestial dragons, that&nbsp;
is burned into her skin, keeps her from truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:34.160
being free. She and her sisters are terrified&nbsp;
tho let anyone know about it and serves as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:39.440
constant reminder and trigger to their horrific&nbsp;
past. The true irony of her character is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.680
that while her charm and even her devil&nbsp;
fruit powers seem to be centered around love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:50.400
lust and romance, she herself is not able to&nbsp;
love or be loved by others. She isn’t even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.880
able to form any meaningful bonds with her own&nbsp;
people, even though she clearly cares for them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.680
deeply as their Queen. After all she took the&nbsp;
step to become a warlord and join hands with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:08.160
very same world government that had caused her so&nbsp;
much pain, just so her people could live in piece.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.080
And so, with the reveal of her backstory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.480
we suddenly see that all the arrogance and&nbsp;
coldness we had seen form her up to that point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.720
is more than just understandable. We as&nbsp;
the reader, have now gone from hating her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:27.040
to feeling empathetic for her. But how then&nbsp;
did that empathy turn into a genuine fondness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:38.720
for her character? The answer, as mostly is&nbsp;
the case, is her relationship with Luffy.

