00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:59.440
As I extensively discussed in&nbsp;
my character analysis of Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.160
his biggest trait is his condition-less altruism.&nbsp;
He sees people’s true hearts and pulls them out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:11.520
their darkness. For someone who has only known&nbsp;
the cruel, egoistic and dominant world of men,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:16.240
Luffy’s approach to life shattered her world&nbsp;
view completely. To illustrate this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.800
take this scene, which I think is one of&nbsp;
the most important for Hancock’s character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:30.400
During the battle in the arena, Luffy covers&nbsp;
her sisters back to prevent her slave mark from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:35.920
being revealed. His rational was that this&nbsp;
didn’t have anything to do with the fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:41.120
and instead of exploiting her weakness, he&nbsp;
chose to respect his enemy’s emotional weakness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:47.920
The past is in the past. Don’t bring it into&nbsp;
present. This act of respect and kindness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.960
deeply resonated with Hancock. To begin&nbsp;
with, she was already shocked that Luffy had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:59.280
no lustful feelings towards her and didn’t treat&nbsp;
her like a Queen of beauty, but like a normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:05.200
person. And now, he had shown her that one’s&nbsp;
past must not necessarily define one’s present.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:09.600
Even though Luffy showed Hancock, that just&nbsp;
like her he had the qualities of a king,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:14.640
he didn’t mind bowing down and pleading for the&nbsp;
life of Margarita, a commoner that he became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.680
friends with. Luffy is a very forgiving person&nbsp;
as he always forgives the mistakes of his crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:25.120
without blinking an eye. Sanji kicked him&nbsp;
in the face until he fell unconscious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:31.520
yet he forgave him. He views his crew-mates as&nbsp;
his friends, not his underlings. Boa Hancock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:37.920
on the other hand, based on her experience, is&nbsp;
not very forgiving. She expects obedience and she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:43.840
expects everyone to live up to her expectations.&nbsp;
We see this even with her own sisters.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:56.640
And yet, as her true self is that of a very kind&nbsp;
and caring person, Luffy’s personality resonated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:02.880
deeply with her. So deeply, that she has fallen&nbsp;
head over heels for him. Not because Luffy is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:09.440
strong, but because of what he stands for and&nbsp;
who he is, which is very genuine love. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:15.760
ironically enough, the only person her love powers&nbsp;
won’t work on, is the one person she genuinely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:21.760
loves. Luffy enables her to show more of her true&nbsp;
and vulnerable self. To from relationships with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:27.120
her people and to let go of her past and embrace&nbsp;
the future. While loving Boa Hancock can turn you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:32.720
to stone, Luffy has taken her own stony heart&nbsp;
and brought it back to life, allowing her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:38.880
trust and love again. This change of heart, pun&nbsp;
absolutely intended, was so intense for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:44.240
that literally fell ill, being overwhelmed with&nbsp;
emotions that she had surpassed for so long.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.040
And so, what makes it almost impossible for us&nbsp;
not to fall in love with her character in return&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:53.680
is the fact that we went from one extreme to&nbsp;
the other with her. At the beginning, Hancock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:59.920
gave us one reason after the next to dislike her.&nbsp;
After falling in love with Luffy, she’s basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:05.920
giving us reason after reason to like her. She&nbsp;
is the one that helps him get into impel down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:11.040
to free his brother. She talked to Ace about him,&nbsp;
covering for him, and she gave Luffy the keys to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:17.040
his handcuffs. And finally, she was the one to&nbsp;
protect him and take him in after Ace’s death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:23.120
and the events of the time skip. All of this was&nbsp;
neither required nor expected of her and it shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:28.960
us, just how genuinely she cares for Luffy with&nbsp;
no ulterior motive. And while some people seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.840
to dislike this innocent and girly side of her,&nbsp;
those of us with a heart understand that this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:39.440
simply the honest side of a traumatized girl that&nbsp;
has started to heal and has fallen in love for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:44.960
first time. And that care she has for Luffy and&nbsp;
the willingness to sacrifice everything for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:52.000
is what makes her so popular. Because her love&nbsp;
for Luffy is an extension of ours for him.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:58.480
Boa Hancock unites all of the core themes and&nbsp;
values of One Piece. Freedom, Love, the cruelness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:05.440
of the world and most importantly, why Luffy is&nbsp;
the one to change it. And with the abolishment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:10.960
of the warlord system, her enormous power and her&nbsp;
relationship with Luffy, I think it’s extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:16.400
likely that she will make a re-appearance&nbsp;
very soon. Oda even hinted at her, Sato and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:22.480
Vivi playing major roles in the story again. So&nbsp;
I think we can all be excited for that. And I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:29.600
recommend you check out my 2 videos on Luffy’s&nbsp;
character here. Thanks for watching. Peace.

